"stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":212444,"global_rank":263606},{"name":"davidbmar/Palindrome-Index","owner":"davidbmar","html_url":"https://github.com/davidbmar/Palindrome-Index","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Given a string, , of lowercase letters, determine the index of the character whose removal will make  a palindrome. If  is already a palindrome or no such character exists, then print . There will always be a valid solution, and any correct answer is acceptable. For example, if  \"bcbc\", we can either remove 'b' at index  or 'c' at index .  Input Format  The first line contains an integer, , denoting the number of test cases.  Each line  of the  subsequent lines (where ) describes a test case in the form of a single string, .  Constraints  All characters are lowercase English letters. Output Format  Print an integer denoting the zero-indexed position of the character that makes  not a palindrome; if  is already a palindrome or no such character exists, print .  Sample Input  3 aaab baa aaa Sample Output  3 0 -1 Explanation  Test Case 1: \"aaab\"  Removing 'b' at index  results in a palindrome, so we print  on a new line.  Test Case 2: \"baa\"  Removing 'b' at index  results in a palindrome, so we print  on a new line.  Test Case 3: \"aaa\"  This string is already a palindrome, so we print ; however, , , and  are also all acceptable answers, as the string will still be a palindrome if any one of the characters at those indices are removed.","topics":[],"score":212440,"global_rank":263615},{"name":"dlauritzen/SqlRest","owner":"dlauritzen","html_url":"https://github.com/dlauritzen/SqlRest","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A super-thin MySQL REST API","topics":[],"score":212434,"global_rank":263630},{"name":"Shuvrima/Neural-Networks","owner":"Shuvrima","html_url":"https://github.com/Shuvrima/Neural-Netw